# System Monitor Sync

When implementing **new website/admin features** that depend on infra, credentials, cron, DB tables, or third-party APIs, also update System Monitor in the **same change** — do not wait for the user to ask.

## Where to update

- API checks: `apps/web/src/app/api/super_admin/system-monitor/route.ts`
- UI icons/labels if new categories: `apps/web/src/app/dashboard/super_admin/system-monitor/page.tsx`
- Wire new check into the `Promise.all([...])` in the GET handler
- Add category weight in `calculateHealthScore` if introducing a new category
- Add related env keys to `envStatus` when the feature needs env/config

## Add a check when the feature involves any of

- New env vars / API keys / service-account credentials
- New cron jobs (`vercel.json` or `/api/cron/*`)
- New critical DB tables/migrations required for the feature to work
- New third-party integrations (WhatsApp, FCM, Razorpay, Maps, AI, telephony, etc.)
- Background senders / queues / scheduled campaigns
- Wallet, coupons, push, RSA, lead distribution, or similar ops modules

## Skip monitor updates for

- Pure UI polish, copy, or layout-only changes
- Refactors with no new dependency or failure mode
- One-off scripts that are not production runtime paths

## Check quality bar

- Return `healthy` | `degraded` | `down` with clear `message` + `reason`
- Prefer real verification (table exists, credentials valid, overdue jobs) over “env var present”
- Include `quickFix` with `internal-link` to the admin page that fixes it when useful
- Keep checks fast; use timeouts; do not break the whole monitor if one optional table is missing (fail that check only)

## Example

If you add scheduled push campaigns + SQL migration `294_*.sql` + cron `/api/cron/scheduled-push`:

1. Add `checkPushCampaigns()` (tables + overdue scheduled rows)
2. Ensure FCM/cron secret checks cover the new path
3. Register the check in GET `Promise.all`
4. Quick-fix link to Advance Notifications / Campaigns
